  "aiContextParagraph": "Discussions regarding the selection of a new vice president to serve alongside President Prabowo Subianto have intensified in Indonesia. Following recent political discourse, various figures have proposed criteria for the role, emphasizing the need for expertise in law and government, as well as the ability to facilitate national consolidation. Among those mentioned by supporters is Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, the current Chairperson of the Gerindra Party and Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives. While some political figures and groups have publicly endorsed his candidacy, others have suggested that the ideal replacement for the position should possess a specific, well-rounded background. Amidst the speculation, it has been noted that the final decision regarding the vice presidential appointment rests entirely with the President. The selection process is expected to culminate in an announcement or formal proceeding by the People's Consultative Assembly scheduled for early December 2026.",
